      "title": "Spain’s PM says no evidence ‘whatsoever’ Morocco behind Ceuta border breach",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/spain-pm-evidence-morocco-ceuta-border-breach",
      "description": "<p>Pedro Sánchez continues to defend Rabat after police report claiming border forces helped 70,000 cross border</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/03/pedro-sanchez-ceuta-migration-crisis-spain-morocco-protests-europe-live-ukraine-russia-italy-latest-news\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Spain has seen no evidence “whatsoever” that Morocco planned or facilitated a mass border breach into its north African territory of Ceuta, the Spanish prime minister, Pedro Sánchez, has told parliament.</p><p>The address on Thursday followed the emergence of a police report, commissioned by a judge and widely quoted in the media, claiming Moroccan border forces had actively aided about 70,000 people to cross the border in late July.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/spain-pm-evidence-morocco-ceuta-border-breach\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T12:52:08"
    },
    {
      "title": "EU’s ability to defend against invasion remains in doubt, finds official report",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/eu-defence-readiness-eca-auditors-us-reliance",
      "description": "<p>Fragmented infrastructure and reliance on US continue to hinder ‘defence readiness’, says European court of auditors</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/03/pedro-sanchez-ceuta-migration-crisis-spain-morocco-protests-europe-live-ukraine-russia-italy-latest-news\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The EU’s ability to respond to a foreign invasion by 2030 remains in doubt due to a continuing reliance on the US and fragmented national defence systems, according to a report from its official auditor.</p><p>The European court of auditors (ECA) said the EU was much better prepared than before Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine of 2022, but achieving its goal of defence readiness by the end of the decade would be difficult.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/eu-defence-readiness-eca-auditors-us-reliance\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T15:09:25"
    },
    {
      "title": "Rise of far-right leader Roberto Vannacci challenges Meloni as she celebrates Italian milestone",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/roberto-vannacci-far-right-party-futuro-nazionale-dilemma-meloni",
      "description": "<p>Futuro Nazionale party’s speedy poll rise poses questions whether PM will return to her roots before election</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/03/pedro-sanchez-ceuta-migration-crisis-spain-morocco-protests-europe-live-ukraine-russia-italy-latest-news\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Giorgia Meloni’s government has become the longest-running in Italy since the second world war – a milestone the prime minister is determined not to let pass unnoticed.</p><p>In the port area of Bari, the capital of the southern Italian region of Puglia, where Meloni hosted the G7 in 2024 and where she spends her summer holiday, preparations are well under way for a festival-style showcase of her rightwing administration.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/roberto-vannacci-far-right-party-futuro-nazionale-dilemma-meloni\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T14:25:25"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘We need a touch of humanity’: Swedish opposition pledges to help Britons facing deportation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/swedish-mp-promises-help-for-britons-facing-deportation-if-his-party-wins-power-general-election",
      "description": "<p>Exclusive: Centre party says it will change law to end plight of those hit by post-Brexit policy if it gains power in upcoming election</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/03/pedro-sanchez-ceuta-migration-crisis-spain-morocco-protests-europe-live-ukraine-russia-italy-latest-news\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>A leading Swedish opposition party has promised an urgent reprieve for British nationals facing deportation from the country over Brexit administrative issues.</p><p>Niels Paarup-Petersen, the migration spokesperson for the Centre party, said it would introduce laws to end the suffering of people <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/10/british-widow-78-told-to-leave-sweden-under-brexit-rules-after-living-there-for-21-years\">such as the 78-year-old British widow Joyce Thomas</a> if, as polls project, it forms a new centre-left coalition after the general election in 10 days’ time. Thomas has been told to leave by next Wednesday after 21 years in Sweden.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/swedish-mp-promises-help-for-britons-facing-deportation-if-his-party-wins-power-general-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T12:38:20"
    },
    {
      "title": "Wife of British man at risk of deportation from Sweden calls on Burnham to intervene",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/wife-of-british-man-at-risk-of-deportation-from-sweden-calls-on-burnham-to-intervene",
      "description": "<p>Case is latest in string of post-Brexit deportations from country, which has been criticised for high refusal rate for British people to remain</p><p>The wife of a British man detained by police in Stockholm on Tuesday ahead of a threatened deportation has pleaded with Andy Burnham to get involved in the Brexit catastrophe unfolding for many British citizens in Sweden.</p><p>Charles, who does not want to be fully identified, and his Swedish wife, Lily, were summoned to the police station at 10am on Tuesday, where he was told he would be held at a detention centre and deported within the next two weeks.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/03/wife-of-british-man-at-risk-of-deportation-from-sweden-calls-on-burnham-to-intervene\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T06:00:45"
    }
  ]
